NODE id=matrix/executor/runtime.coerceArg kind=func
  digest=b3:5b951d85a7da89c3cb5cad945d596e50aaba012360062d28dd8e662682da752e file=executor/runtime/coerce.go range=12:78 lang=go exported=false byte_range=233:2629
  sig=func coerceArg(v string) interface{}
  doc=coerceArg converts a string-typed PlanTree arg into its likely\nJSON-friendly type. ir.ToolCallPayload.Args is map[string]string for\ncanonical hashing simplicity (MCL/ir/plan.go:141), but MCP servers\nexpect ints/bools/objects/arrays per their JSON-Schema inputs.\nBest-effort coercion:\n\n	"true"/"false"        → bool\n	integer string        → int64\n	float string          → float64\n	JSON object "{...}"   → map[string]interface{}\n	JSON array  "[...]"   → []interface{}\n	everything else       → string (verbatim)\n\nThe JSON object/array case is load-bearing for tools whose schema\ndeclares a nested type the plan IR cannot carry directly: the\nplan_tree@1 grammar forces every arg VALUE to a string, so a tool\nlike tachyon_compile (whose `sources` is a map[path]->content) only\never receives its value as a JSON-encoded string. Parsing it back\nhere hands the MCP server the real object instead of a string it\ncannot unmarshal (the prior behavior broke compile/test/deploy/call\nwith a "cannot unmarshal string" error). Same for constructor_args /\nargs arrays and inline abi.\n\nOriginally a verbatim port of cmd/mcl-e2e/walk.go:249-313. The harness\nvalidated this surface against real Fireworks-produced plans + npx/uvx\nMCP servers in sess#22b (75/75 assertions green).
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/executor/runtime/coerce.go

NODE id=matrix/executor/runtime.collectNodeOutputs kind=func
  digest=b3:307c9532dcb7bddd51a2b6360f02e14aa6e1cc4c7e3d58f3ac65a536fb8995b1 file=executor/runtime/argref.go range=42:67 lang=go exported=false byte_range=1945:2767
  sig=func collectNodeOutputs(plan *ir.PlanTree) map[string]string
  doc=collectNodeOutputs walks the plan tree and returns nodeID → recorded runtime\noutput text (PlanNode.ResultText). The walker populates ResultText as steps\nand tool calls complete, so a later node can resolve ${...} references\nagainst the real upstream output. Mirrors the cmd/mcl-execute helper of the\nsame name (which feeds NodeStep inputs); kept here so the runtime walker can\nresolve NodeToolCall args without importing package main.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/executor/runtime/argref.go

NODE id=matrix/executor/runtime.containsCodeFence kind=func
  digest=b3:0ae11f366369351274b56a786bfc20df3fc51c47caa6c8d106a797fe0c94ac31 file=executor/runtime/coerce.go range=160:163 lang=go exported=false byte_range=5743:5889
  sig=func containsCodeFence(s string) bool
  doc=containsCodeFence reports whether s carries a Markdown code fence.
